id: pm-lint-incremental-invalidation
title: Preserve complete lint results with incremental rule invalidation
description: "Retain rule dependency metadata and SDK event cursors to update a complete lint result after unrelated edits. Overlap recheck: existing lint --since filters items by updated_at and drops other findings; lint baselines acknowledge findings without skipping evaluation; portable rule packs and repair previews do not maintain an incremental result. Core listMutationEvents supplies pagination and listAllComplete/certifyCompleteListResult supplies complete corpus certification. Sibling pm-observer cursors track evidence ingestion and pm-graph refreshes graph projections; neither owns lint rule/item dependency invalidation."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-27T08:23:52.579Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T12:27:44.404Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "One title edit in 10000 items reruns only affected rules plus declared global checks; the complete result equals a fresh full scan; cursor loss or rule-version drift forces an explicit rebuild; typed SDK and CLI, compact TOON/JSON, typed refusals, README and example, public non-git tracker validation, seeded state properties and interleaving coverage, npm and Bun CI release gates."
parent: pm-lint-epic
comments[15]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T08:31:39.266Z",codex-agent,"Implemented an SDK-injected incremental engine and a fenced file adapter. Checkpoints keep native-source digests, declared per-rule input digests, violation bits and an SDK cursor anchor; findings are freshly rendered from a certified full read. Global checks are clock, hierarchy, blocker references and SDK duplicates. Core leases serialize checkpoint reads and publication; every source revision and policy is read back through the SDK before publishing. No item mutations or journaled item plans are introduced. Registry version lookup reports 2026.10.27; the repository SDK pin remains 2026.10.23 as required."
  "2026-10-27T08:55:08.856Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public origin/main tracker validation: 21 items, zero findings, source digest 16b7a56ee139b2681ce3ece7e468d9caea102b1cd32a38f9aee4ee638ffaa7d1; authoritative names and bytes preserved. No-op: 12 global predicates, 54 reused pairs. One title edit on a separate disposable derivative: 15 evaluated, 51 reused; result equals fresh full scan. Observed milliseconds: rebuild 3650, no-op 694, edit 288, fresh full 98; incremental reduces predicate work, not every wall-time cost. Seed 0x1ace2026 passed 500 native-state/checkpoint sequences and the second property passed 500 random custom registries. Schema, fenced publication, real 1000-event pagination and all interleaving tests pass. Rule version advances to 2 for lifecycle-role semantics; old baseline documents remain readable and stale acknowledgments are explicit."
  "2026-10-27T09:01:28.248Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replacing only the incremental evaluator cache decision with false makes the focused equality/reuse regression fail (PML001 evaluated 2 instead of 1; reused 0 instead of 1). Restored the function immediately. Focused coverage run: 36 tests passed, zero failures; all five incremental modules, status adapter and rule predicates reached 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines in that measured scope. Full package coverage and packed npm/Bun consumer gates remain CI evidence. The registered pm test run executes the nine real incremental regressions on non-git trackers."
  "2026-10-27T09:04:46.797Z",codex-agent,"Registered pm regression run passed all nine incremental tests with no failure categories. The focused measured source set has four incremental implementation modules plus the status adapter at 100 percent in every coverage dimension; the full CI gate supplies package-wide counts and thresholds. Read-only cache evaluation performs no native create/update/import/sync, so ambient create scope, revision-bound idempotency keys and journaled item plans are not introduced. Core events, complete-list certification, lifecycle registry, duplication analysis, leases and atomic publication are reused."
  "2026-10-27T09:17:35.610Z",codex-agent,"PR ready for review: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/pull/32 . CI release gate: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/actions/runs/40479011342 (queued at recording time; PR checks carry the current-head continuation). Compatibility check of the published 2026.10.20 SDK declarations confirms acquireLockLease is absent from its public runtime, index and lock declarations. Raise peer and manifest host minimum to the already pinned/tested 2026.10.23; keep the development SDK pin unchanged. Implementation and targeted acceptance are complete; CI runner scheduling remains external verification. Item stays in progress for orchestrator verification and closure."
  "2026-10-27T09:33:42.564Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance on the final implementation passed: npm run test:install; 1 integration test, 1 pass, 0 fail/skip/cancel/todo, duration 515980 ms. It executes packed SDK and CLI paths through npm global, Bun global, npx, native bunx and direct project-local entrypoints. Full release CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/actions/runs/40479849595 is still queued with both Node 22 and Node 26 jobs and no executed gate steps; no full npm/Bun release-gate pass is claimed. The PR checks page tracks the latest receipt-only commit. Functional acceptance and measured public validation are documented; final external gate verification remains for the pipeline."
  "2026-10-27T09:50:32.483Z",codex-agent,"Re-review class audit: (1) compare-and-publish decisions must be revalidated after every awaited preparation/SDK/lease step, with no asynchronous gap between final target identity/content comparison and replacement; (2) replacement files must never widen target access permissions, and new cache/evidence files default to owner-only. Package-wide search finds two durable sidecar writers: incremental checkpoints and baseline acknowledgments. Baselines also have a read/write/sync/rename gap and lock-path cleanup risk, so both writers will share the corrected publisher. Repair previews and witness/rule-pack commands do not publish durable sidecars. The branch is current with origin/main (three commits ahead, zero behind). Reclaiming this item for the corrections; no published inline non-blocking findings were available."
  "2026-10-27T10:14:25.231Z",codex-agent,"Class fixes implemented in one publisher shared by checkpoint and baseline writers. Private 0600 staging remains private until final publication; existing access bits, UID and GID are preserved. The final file-generation/byte/metadata comparison and rename are synchronous inside the held lease/lock after all awaited SDK, staging and lease-fence setup. Cleanup verifies staging inode ownership. Exact file revisions intentionally detect whitespace-only and identical-byte inode replacements; this is an artifact revision comparison, not a semantic input comparison. SDK writeFileAtomic exposes only createParentDirectories, with no expected generation or access-policy parameters, so core leases/fencing are retained and the missing final primitive is package-owned. New focused run passed 18 tests and shared publisher coverage is 100/100/100/100. Function-only reverts each fail behaviorally: old checkpoint writer returns success after final-policy foreign replacement and creates 0666 under umask 000; old baseline publisher returns success after foreign replacement during sync and changes 0400 to 0600. Functions restored after each proof. Added packed npm/Bun SDK race cases and permission checks across global, npx/bunx and local CLI paths."
  "2026-10-27T10:16:10.331Z",codex-agent,"Final function-only revert receipts: restoring only lintIncrementalFile produces a successful return after the final-policy foreign write (regression: missing expected rejection) and checkpoint creation mode 0666 rather than 0600 under umask 000. Restoring only publishBaseline produces a successful return after a foreign write during durable sync and changes baseline mode 0400 to 0600. All four reverted runs exit 1 on behavioral assertions, then the current functions were restored. Additional focused coverage is 18/18, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo; shared publisher is 100/100/100/100. Original baseline regressions remain intact. Next: registered publication test, then serial full npm and Bun release gates with isolated HOME, git identity config disabled and at most two test workers."
  "2026-10-27T10:37:20.455Z",codex-agent,"The broader ownership audit also caught in-place foreign edits of our staging inode: inode-only cleanup would delete that data. Cleanup now verifies owned bytes/prefix and the access policy this invocation actually applied, preserving foreign content, foreign metadata and unreadable/oversized unknown records. Restoring only removeOwnedStage from the prior commit makes the adversarial test fail with the foreign staging payload deleted (ENOENT); the current cleanup passes for checkpoint and baseline writers. Focused publication/baseline run is now 21/21, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo, and shared publisher coverage is 100/100/100/100. The superseded npm full gate was deliberately stopped before completion for this class correction; it is not passing evidence. Restarting both full gates serially on the completed fix."
  "2026-10-27T10:45:34.265Z",codex-agent,"Completed focused validation: 31/31 tests passed, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo; baseline-file, incremental-file and sidecar-publication each measure 100/100/100/100. Added explicit adapter fault injection to verify newly opened handles are closed when metadata reads fail; this also covers the checkpoint preparation refusal without any publication. Full release gates now restart on the frozen completed source. No additional published inline/non-blocking review findings were present in PR metadata; the two supplied blockers and the class-wide baseline/staging ownership defects are addressed."
  "2026-10-27T11:55:13.347Z",codex-agent,"Full release gates PASS serially at source 208f70fe1715ade3a00d1bf0c13a8d15da6a34ae: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 179 main tests plus 1 packed integration, with zero fail/skip/cancel/todo and 100/100/100/100 across all 30 measured source files. Maximum test concurrency was two; thresholds unchanged. Isolated home and Git configuration reproduced CI identity. npm elapsed 1804238 ms; Bun 2292750 ms; packed legs 454550/424134 ms. Both include npm global, Bun global, npx/native bunx, project-local CLI and packed SDK permission/race assertions. Merged origin/main 815ec63 tracker-only closure evidence after the running gates finished; product source, tests, scripts and dependencies are byte-identical to 208f70f. The earlier pre-fix CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/actions/runs/40481767791 also completed successfully: Node 22 npm and Node 26 npm/Bun each 167 main plus 1 packed test, 100/100/100/100 over 29 files; this is historical evidence, not approval of the new fixes. Final pushed-head evidence will be linked at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/pull/32/checks. No additional published review findings were present. All five behavioral revert proofs and the package-wide class audit are recorded above."
  "2026-10-27T11:55:31.116Z",codex-agent,"Post-merge linked-test receipt: pm test pm-lint-incremental-invalidation --run --match publication.test.ts --progress --timeout 300 passed all 22 publication/baseline tests in 8482 ms; zero fail/skip/cancel/todo. All review changes are complete and the claim is released for pushed-head CI and orchestrator re-review. No item is closed; no merge or release of the PR is authorized."
  "2026-10-27T11:56:28.570Z",codex-agent,"Final integration checks: origin/main merged cleanly; linked publication/baseline test run passed 22/22. Changelog regenerated and verified; identity gate reports zero violations. Unisolated pm health was refused by an unrelated globally enabled pm-github extension built for host 2026.10.27 while the package pins 2026.10.23. With isolated HOME and Git configuration, strict pm health --require-merge-drivers passes all authority/storage/history checks (only an advisory pending telemetry entry); no global configuration or dependency pin was changed. This is an ambient installation skew, not an open finding in the package. The feature remains in_progress with its claim released."
  "2026-10-27T12:27:44.402Z",codex-agent,"Bounded CI watch reached the queue rules approximately 30-minute cap after pushing 74774aba9b9e90df4828de739293184f81ffa5c1. CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/actions/runs/40499927461 still has test (22) and test (26) queued, with zero executed steps and zero completed full gates on this watched head. CodeQL https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/actions/runs/40499927369 is also queued. No new CI pass is claimed. Local npm/Bun gates remain green: each 179 main plus 1 packed test, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo, 100/100/100/100. New PR review threads/submissions remain absent; skipped and unavailable bot reviews are missing evidence, not approval. All supplied findings and the durable-publication class are fixed with five behavioral revert proofs. This final receipt changes only tracker/docs evidence; its subsequent CI is visible at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/pull/32/checks. The orchestrator pipeline must wait for final checks and re-review before merging. The claim remains released and the item in_progress."
